[list]
[*]Floor borders no longer carry the setting Ideology reads as marking a building only some ideoligions may build. v1.1.3 let every ideoligion build them in spite of it; now nothing in the game or in another mod treats them as ideoligion buildings. Every colonist builds them, as since v1.1.3, and the build menu is unchanged: one button per shape, with every style on its right-click menu.
[*]For mod authors: a border another mod adds no longer sets canGenerateDefaultDesignator to false to join its shape's button, since Neat Edges now keeps the game's own buttons for borders off the tabs itself. A border that still sets it is named in a warning at startup, because Ideology would read it as an ideoligion building. The README on GitHub has the details.
[*]Unchanged: Neat Edges still requires only Harmony, no defs were added or renamed, and nothing new is saved. Hard edges, areas and borders already in your saves load as they are and harden the same edges.
[/list]
